WEBVTT

00:05.420 --> 00:06.990
It's the lake!

01:38.240 --> 01:41.990
Episode 5

01:38.240 --> 01:41.990
First Official Trip

01:42.760 --> 01:44.240
Official trip?

01:44.240 --> 01:45.220
Yes.

01:45.220 --> 01:48.340
It's a request from someone 
who used to come to worship quite often,

01:48.340 --> 01:51.350
but her legs have gotten worse, 
so it's difficult for her to go out now.

01:51.350 --> 01:53.770
She said that she knows 
it will be a bit of a trip,

01:53.770 --> 01:55.340
but she hopes I'll come anyway.

01:55.590 --> 01:58.850
I was wondering if the two 
of you would like to come.

02:00.600 --> 02:03.980
I didn't know that lakes are so clear!

02:03.980 --> 02:05.460
It's the first time I've seen one!

02:05.460 --> 02:07.880
Abel, you look pale.

02:07.880 --> 02:09.170
I got sick on the carriage.

02:09.170 --> 02:11.230
Welcome, young Lawrence!

02:11.950 --> 02:14.490
Miss Corrine. It's good to see you again.

02:14.490 --> 02:17.920
It's been years since the last 
time we saw each other, hasn't it?

02:17.920 --> 02:19.740
Yes, it has.

02:19.740 --> 02:21.770
I'm sorry to ask you all the way out here.

02:21.770 --> 02:24.420
You must have had to close the church.

02:24.420 --> 02:26.400
Please don't worry about any of that.

02:26.400 --> 02:29.960
And there aren't many opportunities 
for the lady saint to go on a long trip.

02:29.960 --> 02:31.850
Truth be told, we're grateful.

02:31.850 --> 02:35.060
Lawren! Fish! There are fish!

02:35.060 --> 02:40.760
Oh! There's some over here, too! 
There are fish here!

02:35.070 --> 02:38.000
I very much wanted to give her a long trip.

02:38.000 --> 02:40.770
You're living with her 
right now, aren't you?

02:40.770 --> 02:43.420
This is the first time 
I've met a lady saint.

02:43.420 --> 02:45.270
That's the case for most people.

02:45.270 --> 02:46.770
There are so many!

02:47.270 --> 02:49.450
An adorable young lady, isn't she?

02:49.640 --> 02:50.940
Yes, she is.

02:54.250 --> 02:57.060
I got a little overexcited.

02:57.060 --> 03:00.830
Until now, I'd never seen anything 
more than the village river.

03:00.830 --> 03:03.670
Then please look to your heart's content!

03:03.670 --> 03:07.240
After all, this place has
become a sightseeing spot.

03:07.240 --> 03:09.240
Now that I think about it, 
a book I read talked

03:09.240 --> 03:11.080
about the overwhelming 
beauty of this place...

03:11.080 --> 03:14.920
It called it something like, 
"The Lake of Fairies."

03:14.920 --> 03:18.140
Miss, hearing you say such fantastical 
things cracks me up.

03:18.140 --> 03:20.220
You just rest!

03:20.220 --> 03:25.580
I never imagined you'd bring 
all these friends, Lawrence.

03:25.580 --> 03:27.480
I'm sorry there are so many of us.

03:27.480 --> 03:28.970
No, that isn't what I meant.

03:28.970 --> 03:31.720
I feel better because you aren't alone.

03:31.980 --> 03:37.620
Your grandfather, Mister Oswell, 
would feel the same, I think.

03:37.620 --> 03:39.580
Lawren will never be alone!

03:39.580 --> 03:41.370
I won't allow it!

03:41.370 --> 03:42.620
My, my.

03:42.850 --> 03:45.660
Your bags must be heavy. 
Let me show you the way.

03:45.660 --> 03:49.090
The lady saint and I will be 
conducting a service now.

03:49.090 --> 03:51.610
Miss Hazelita, will you stay 
with Abel for me?

03:51.610 --> 03:53.170
All right.

03:53.570 --> 03:56.670
You really have grown up splendidly.

03:56.670 --> 03:58.540
What's this all of a sudden?

03:58.540 --> 04:02.400
When you were little you 
were energetic and earnest.

04:02.400 --> 04:04.340
You'd run around all over the place.

04:04.340 --> 04:06.870
Really, such a mischievous child!

04:07.810 --> 04:11.640
You'd do things like force your way close 
to cats and get punched for it.

04:11.640 --> 04:12.470
I see. I see!

04:12.470 --> 04:16.400
And sometimes, Mister Oswell would get angry 
with you for interrupting his work.

04:16.400 --> 04:18.370
Let's please not talk about that.

04:18.370 --> 04:19.920
It makes me want to run and hide.

04:19.920 --> 04:22.240
I'm having fun, though.

04:23.130 --> 04:27.100
You can just leave me here 
and have a look around, you know?

04:27.100 --> 04:28.550
As long as you don't get lost.

04:28.550 --> 04:30.390
I would never get lost!

04:30.390 --> 04:34.130
Now that I think about it... 
I brought a camera.

04:35.970 --> 04:37.950
And that. And this, too.

04:38.730 --> 04:39.710
Come on, now.

04:40.020 --> 04:42.470
Miss, where are you going?

04:45.360 --> 04:48.220
That... wasn't a fish, was it?

04:48.220 --> 04:51.760
Huh? Where am I? Abel!

04:52.170 --> 04:54.110
I did tell her.

04:54.550 --> 04:55.870
Oh, dear.

04:55.870 --> 04:58.110
I have to start getting dinner ready!

04:58.110 --> 05:00.430
I'll go make dinner.

05:00.430 --> 05:02.430
You two, please stay and relax.

05:02.430 --> 05:03.360
Really?

05:03.360 --> 05:05.620
I suppose I'll leave it to you, then.

05:05.880 --> 05:06.990
Oh, yes.

05:06.990 --> 05:09.870
Mister Oswell wasn't very good at cooking,

05:09.870 --> 05:12.880
so Lawrence was always making their meals.

05:12.880 --> 05:16.320
Though I heard he struggled quite 
a bit in the beginning.

05:18.960 --> 05:20.810
He hasn't changed at all.

05:20.810 --> 05:22.470
He hasn't?

05:22.650 --> 05:27.500
He has grown up, of course, 
but he's just the same at his core.

05:27.830 --> 05:30.480
He's always been a kind boy.

05:31.720 --> 05:32.640
Is something wrong?

05:32.640 --> 05:34.230
What? Oh, um...

05:34.230 --> 05:39.020
Hearing you compliment Lawren 
just made me feel so happy.

05:39.020 --> 05:42.950
You really do love him, don't you?

05:42.950 --> 05:44.090
Lo—

05:44.090 --> 05:45.370
Miss Corinne?

05:45.370 --> 05:47.540
I'm sorry, I'm not used to 
where things are here.

05:47.540 --> 05:48.890
I'll be right there!

05:50.420 --> 05:53.660
A lot of your smiles have 
seemed suspicious today.

05:54.560 --> 05:58.540
Wow, you can see the lake 
from the windows. How lovely!

05:58.540 --> 05:59.920
Y-Yes.

05:59.920 --> 06:01.420
Is something wrong?

06:02.260 --> 06:05.680
I wasn't planning on talking 
about this today,

06:05.990 --> 06:08.980
but at night, even though there 
isn't anyone else here,

06:08.980 --> 06:11.840
I hear voices speaking from the lake.

06:12.090 --> 06:13.100
Voices?

06:13.100 --> 06:15.600
They say that fairies live there.

06:15.600 --> 06:18.760
It makes me wonder if perhaps they 
aren't human voices.

06:18.760 --> 06:22.100
A long time ago, I asked Mister Oswell 
to come here to consult about it,

06:22.100 --> 06:24.320
and the voices stopped for a while.

06:25.540 --> 06:28.000
He was an unusual person, remember?

06:28.000 --> 06:31.530
It was as though he could see things 
that regular people couldn't.

06:31.530 --> 06:34.920
He seemed to advise on these 
kinds of issues quite often.

06:35.540 --> 06:38.740
<i>Grandpa did that sort of thing?</i>

06:39.900 --> 06:43.430
So, what picture did you take 
that was worth getting lost over?

06:43.430 --> 06:45.960
I-It was a picture of a squirrel.

06:45.960 --> 06:48.130
There are squirrels 
where you live, aren't there?

06:48.130 --> 06:51.280
Um, I haven't seen Lawren around.

06:51.280 --> 06:53.390
He said he was going out for a little while.

06:53.390 --> 06:57.180
I see. I'll go look for him.

06:57.180 --> 07:00.320
Don't you think you should
be photographing the lake?

07:00.320 --> 07:02.370
Of course I tried to take pictures of it.

07:02.370 --> 07:06.320
But for some reason, and only for pictures 
of the lake, the shutter wouldn't close.

07:06.320 --> 07:08.060
"The shutter wouldn't"...

07:08.060 --> 07:12.180
Miss Corinne, is it common 
to not be able to take pictures here?

07:12.180 --> 07:13.200
No.

07:13.200 --> 07:15.830
People take lots of lovely 
pictures of the scenery.

07:16.640 --> 07:18.320
I see.

07:18.630 --> 07:20.840
<i>That splash.</i>

07:20.840 --> 07:25.620
<i>Does it mean that something 
in the lake is more restless than usual?</i>

07:25.940 --> 07:30.280
<i>The person who would be most 
affected by something like that is...</i>

07:32.280 --> 07:35.420
<i>There weren't any signs 
that anyone else is in the area.</i>

07:35.860 --> 07:37.040
<i>Does that mean...</i>

07:37.040 --> 07:39.670
<i>there really is something 
here that I can't see?</i>

07:40.130 --> 07:41.440
If that's true...

07:41.700 --> 07:42.980
then I can't...

07:48.560 --> 07:49.660
Lawren!

07:54.130 --> 07:56.380
Lady Saint, are you all right?

07:56.380 --> 07:57.540
Lady Saint!

07:59.780 --> 08:02.800
I-I-I'm all right! What about you, Lawren?

08:04.590 --> 08:05.490
<i>What was that?</i>

08:05.490 --> 08:07.040
Thank you.

08:07.220 --> 08:10.540
I was thinking about something 
and seem to have lost my footing.

08:10.540 --> 08:11.820
Thinking about something?

08:11.820 --> 08:14.020
It wasn't anything important!

08:14.050 --> 08:15.340
<b>Stare...</b>

08:16.020 --> 08:20.600
Um, it really isn't anything important.

08:21.070 --> 08:24.400
I was raised by my 
grandfather. He was a pastor.

08:24.400 --> 08:27.140
But he passed away a few years ago.

08:27.140 --> 08:32.210
I vowed to look after 
the church in my grandfather's place,

08:32.900 --> 08:34.320
but it's no good.

08:34.320 --> 08:36.040
It seems it will be difficult 
for me to become

08:36.040 --> 08:38.160
like my grandfather for a long time to come.

08:38.160 --> 08:42.380
I've put myself through many things in 
an effort to get even a little closer to him,

08:42.380 --> 08:45.120
but some things are impossible 
no matter what you try.

08:46.260 --> 08:49.010
We spoke about it earlier, didn't we?

08:49.620 --> 08:54.040
Your grandfather wasn't good 
at cooking, so you did it instead.

08:54.040 --> 08:56.020
Huh? What about it?

08:56.020 --> 09:00.340
There are things that your grandfather 
could do that you can't, Lawren,

09:00.340 --> 09:04.950
but there are things that you can do 
that your grandfather couldn't.

09:04.950 --> 09:06.720
It's just cooking. It isn't all that—

09:06.720 --> 09:09.450
Your cooking is important, 
Lawren! Very important!

09:10.060 --> 09:12.500
Carrying on his work is 
a worthy thing to do.

09:12.500 --> 09:18.080
But fretting because you can't be 
like someone else is a bit of a waste.

09:18.950 --> 09:25.280
Lawren, you can protect that church 
and its people in your own way, can't you?

09:25.600 --> 09:30.140
And if there's ever anything 
that you can't do on your own,

09:30.480 --> 09:33.300
then the people around you will help you.

09:33.730 --> 09:38.480
It might even be that that's what 
your grandfather was hoping for.

09:38.480 --> 09:42.530
How is it that you know the kinds 
of things my grandfather might say?

09:42.530 --> 09:47.440
Since he's the one who raised you, 
I thought he must have been a kind person.

09:47.620 --> 09:51.200
I'll never let you be alone,

09:51.200 --> 09:55.010
so I hope you won't ever 
make me be alone, either.

09:55.010 --> 09:55.940
Because...

09:55.940 --> 09:58.480
I-I can't do housework and things.

09:59.570 --> 10:01.960
You laughed! You're laughing, aren't you?

10:01.960 --> 10:05.340
Well, when you say these things, 
Lady Saint, they sound convincing.

10:05.860 --> 10:06.960
You're right.

10:06.960 --> 10:09.920
Everyone has things they're bad at 
and things they're good at.

10:10.590 --> 10:12.140
<i>I understand!</i>

10:12.430 --> 10:15.600
<i>Until now, I'd never thought of 
relying on anyone else, but...</i>

10:16.300 --> 10:19.130
Lady Saint, I would like 
to ask you about something.

10:19.750 --> 10:23.480
I see. Voices coming from this lake.

10:23.700 --> 10:26.970
So, when you almost fell 
into the lake just now,

10:26.970 --> 10:29.240
did you notice anything strange?

10:29.240 --> 10:32.440
Now that you ask, I did feel 
like my arm was being pulled.

10:32.440 --> 10:33.440
Really?

10:33.840 --> 10:36.060
I understand everything now.

10:37.030 --> 10:39.720
Is there something here?

10:39.720 --> 10:40.640
Yes.

10:40.640 --> 10:44.130
It's just as the name, "The Lake 
of Fairies," implies.

10:44.130 --> 10:48.170
By nature, they are free-spirited 
and irrational,

10:48.170 --> 10:52.840
but not everything they do 
can be permitted in our world.

10:53.110 --> 10:55.000
Please leave this to me.

10:55.000 --> 10:57.510
<i>Is the lady saint angry?</i>

10:57.510 --> 10:59.640
Hey, Lawrence?

10:59.640 --> 11:01.320
Are you all right?

11:04.800 --> 11:06.640
Did something happen?

11:07.580 --> 11:09.870
I nearly fell in the lake.

11:09.870 --> 11:10.640
What?

11:10.640 --> 11:14.570
That was a very close call! 
You have to be sure to be careful!

11:14.570 --> 11:15.400
Yes, I will.

11:15.870 --> 11:18.760
Saint Cecilia, this lake is...

11:18.760 --> 11:21.400
There are some naughty little ones here.

11:21.400 --> 11:23.080
Thought so.

11:23.080 --> 11:27.590
This afternoon, Miss turned her camera on 
the lake, but the shutter wouldn't close.

11:27.590 --> 11:32.400
And it seems Lawrence nearly 
got taken away by them.

11:33.340 --> 11:36.580
Abel, you have a cross 
made of iron, don't you?

11:36.580 --> 11:37.670
Please let me borrow it.

11:37.670 --> 11:39.670
As a measure against fairies?

11:39.670 --> 11:42.440
Saint Cecilia, you don't need 
that kind of thing, do you?

11:42.440 --> 11:43.670
Lady Saint?

11:44.140 --> 11:47.150
May I ask you for a favor?

11:47.150 --> 11:49.150
You want to watch?

11:49.150 --> 11:49.890
Yes.

11:49.890 --> 11:53.770
I want to watch whatever you're 
about to do from behind you.

11:53.770 --> 11:56.780
What? It isn't interesting or anything!

11:56.780 --> 12:00.580
All you'll be able to see is what looks 
like me talking to the air and water!

12:00.580 --> 12:02.160
Even so, I'd like to watch.

12:02.160 --> 12:05.610
I'm already leaving everything 
to you, Lady Saint.

12:05.610 --> 12:09.370
I would at least like to be 
able to watch until it's finished.

12:10.810 --> 12:14.240
You really are a serious one, 
aren't you, Lawren?

12:14.240 --> 12:15.920
Why are you laughing?

12:15.920 --> 12:17.630
In return for earlier.

12:17.630 --> 12:19.390
In that case, Lawren...

12:19.390 --> 12:21.870
please watch until the work is finished.

12:22.920 --> 12:24.130
I will!

12:31.450 --> 12:35.610
Fairies who live 
in the lake, listen closely.

12:35.970 --> 12:37.820
If you wish to be riotous,

12:37.820 --> 12:41.120
please do so in the middle of the lake, 
where there are no people.

12:41.120 --> 12:45.870
<i>It really does seem like she's 
speaking to the air and the water.</i>

12:46.520 --> 12:52.620
<i>I can't see them, but for the lady saint, 
these beings' existence is normal.</i>

12:53.510 --> 12:57.380
<i>Did Grandpa do this same sort of thing, too?</i>

12:57.800 --> 13:01.590
<i>Seeing her as she usually is, 
I nearly forget...</i>

13:02.030 --> 13:06.200
<i>but the lady saint really 
is someone who protects people.</i>

13:09.760 --> 13:12.830
Last night, I didn't hear any voices at all!

13:12.830 --> 13:14.640
Thanks to that, I slept very deeply.

13:14.640 --> 13:16.760
Thank you for everything, truly.

13:16.760 --> 13:19.290
No, thank you for taking care of us.

13:19.290 --> 13:23.280
I'd like to visit the church again one day.

13:23.280 --> 13:27.270
So keep working hard, 
won't you, young Lawrence?

13:27.270 --> 13:30.320
If anything happens, 
I'll be there to help you.

13:31.250 --> 13:33.160
Thank you.

13:35.410 --> 13:38.440
Miss, the carriage stop is straight ahead.

13:38.440 --> 13:39.770
Just keep going straight.

13:39.770 --> 13:42.670
I won't get lost when there's only one path!

13:42.670 --> 13:46.090
You're the one who should be concentrating 
on not getting sick this time!

13:46.090 --> 13:48.640
Are you still sleepy, Lady Saint?

13:48.640 --> 13:49.800
Yes.

13:49.800 --> 13:53.760
Last night, for some reason, 
we started to simply chat.

13:53.760 --> 13:57.310
I wasn't expecting the fairies 
to enjoy talking so much.

13:57.570 --> 14:00.810
<i>But what was even more unexpected...</i>

14:01.120 --> 14:06.570
<i>was for Lawren to indicate his understanding 
about me interacting with fairies.</i>

14:06.950 --> 14:13.450
<i>I wonder if the time will come that I can 
tell you about your unusual predisposition.</i>

14:13.780 --> 14:14.930
Lady Saint?

14:14.930 --> 14:19.200
Were you that angry because it seemed like 
they were trying to drop me into the lake?

14:19.200 --> 14:21.070
Yes, I was!

14:21.070 --> 14:22.800
So, that was the reason.

14:22.800 --> 14:24.500
I'm sorry to have made you worry.

14:24.690 --> 14:27.850
I've never seen you 
angry before, Lady Saint,

14:27.850 --> 14:31.040
so I've been wondering about 
the reason for it all this time.

14:31.040 --> 14:33.640
<i>Lawren is so dense, but he figured it out.</i>

14:33.640 --> 14:38.390
As I thought, I really can't 
ever let you be alone, Lawren.

14:39.200 --> 14:40.950
What's that about?

14:41.980 --> 14:43.000
It's this way.

14:42.980 --> 14:45.980
In a way, it's a sort of talent.

14:43.000 --> 14:44.510
Miss, stop.

14:46.990 --> 14:49.990
Fairies don't like iron.

14:53.650 --> 14:55.870
You're pretty good at this.

14:55.870 --> 14:58.870
Actually, today is February fourteenth.

14:58.870 --> 15:01.280
Aren't you going to do 
anything for Valentine's?

15:01.280 --> 15:03.680
What's Valentine's?

15:05.670 --> 15:08.170
Such a wonderful cultural custom exists?

15:08.170 --> 15:11.010
Lawrence didn't teach you about it?

15:11.010 --> 15:12.220
No.

15:12.220 --> 15:16.880
Worst case, it's possible that Lawren 
doesn't know about this event either.

15:16.880 --> 15:20.120
No, he's received lots of chocolates 
ever since we were in school,

15:20.120 --> 15:21.430
so he knows about it.

15:22.410 --> 15:24.150
It's all right!

15:24.150 --> 15:27.360
The fact that he's single 
right now says it all.

15:27.360 --> 15:30.820
More importantly, 
what will you do? It's today.

15:31.260 --> 15:34.500
And I don't know how to make chocolates.

15:34.500 --> 15:39.240
There's a way to use Valentine's 
as the reason to spend the day together!

15:39.240 --> 15:41.180
You could ask him to teach you!

15:41.180 --> 15:42.620
You complete idiot!

15:42.970 --> 15:44.310
What are you trying to do?

15:44.310 --> 15:49.180
Giving him chocolates isn't going to 
make him realize how she feels, is it?

15:49.180 --> 15:51.800
Saint Cecilia needs a chance 
to give them to him her own way.

15:51.800 --> 15:53.940
You three seem to be having fun.

15:53.940 --> 15:55.260
What are you doing?

15:55.260 --> 15:57.480
W-Well...

15:57.920 --> 16:01.320
Oh, now that you mention it, 
today <i>is</i> Valentine's!

16:01.320 --> 16:04.070
It seems Cecilia didn't know about it.

16:04.070 --> 16:05.420
Really?

16:05.420 --> 16:06.480
I'm sorry.

16:06.480 --> 16:08.940
It isn't a day I pay much attention to, 
so I didn't think of it.

16:08.940 --> 16:12.510
B-But I heard that you received 
a lot of chocolates.

16:12.510 --> 16:15.000
Why was that?

16:15.000 --> 16:17.790
Everyone wanted me to repay 
the gift on White Day.

16:17.790 --> 16:18.610
What?

16:18.610 --> 16:20.740
They would say, "You have to 
repay me five-fold,"

16:20.740 --> 16:23.000
so I'd make something elaborate 
to give back to them.

16:23.000 --> 16:26.040
Was there a different 
event just for Lawrence?

16:26.040 --> 16:29.000
An event where he bestows 
desserts, it seems.

16:29.000 --> 16:31.500
And what about after you become a pastor?

16:31.500 --> 16:34.260
I've received several since then, I think.

16:34.260 --> 16:37.170
<i>Lawren is... so popular.</i>

16:37.170 --> 16:40.940
Learning how to make chocolates 
from Lawrence himself on Valentine's...

16:40.940 --> 16:45.180
now, that's something I think 
only you can do, Saint Cecilia.

16:45.180 --> 16:47.740
Please teach me how to make chocolates!

16:47.740 --> 16:48.440
What?

16:49.940 --> 16:53.320
Lady Saint, do you have someone 
you'd like to give them to?

16:53.320 --> 16:55.400
Um, well...

16:55.400 --> 16:56.680
Oh,

16:56.680 --> 17:00.130
it's just I never imagined that you might 
have someone like that, so I didn't notice!

17:00.130 --> 17:01.010
All right.

17:01.010 --> 17:03.840
If it's something simple, I think 
you'll be able to make it right away.

17:03.840 --> 17:06.030
<i>To think he's really this dense.</i>

17:06.030 --> 17:08.360
Whoa, there. Miss, heel.

17:11.850 --> 17:14.630
<i>Now that things have turned out 
this way, I'll do my very best!</i>

17:14.630 --> 17:15.400
Oh.

17:15.400 --> 17:18.810
Have Abel and Miss 
Hazelita gone out somewhere?

17:18.810 --> 17:23.020
The way things are going, Abel said he 
wasn't sure what Hazelita might do to you,

17:23.020 --> 17:25.360
so he took her outside.

17:25.360 --> 17:26.970
What does that mean?

17:28.730 --> 17:30.480
<b>1 hour later</b>

17:32.230 --> 17:36.610
Is it possible that I have 
absolutely no aptitude for sculpting?

17:36.610 --> 17:37.670
I know!

17:37.670 --> 17:41.530
They say that it helps to think of the 
person you want to give it to, don't they?

17:43.040 --> 17:45.850
<i>My person is right 
in front of me, so why...?</i>

17:46.540 --> 17:49.400
Lady Saint, we seem 
to be nearly out of ingredients,

17:49.400 --> 17:50.790
so I'll go out and buy some more.

17:50.790 --> 17:53.800
A-All right. Sorry for the trouble.

18:01.200 --> 18:03.050
<i>Who could it be?</i>

18:03.790 --> 18:07.770
So, what did you mean by 
"give them to him her own way"?

18:07.770 --> 18:11.690
He may not know who she's making them for,

18:11.690 --> 18:17.130
but seeing Saint Cecilia working 
so hard will make Lawrence think.

18:17.130 --> 18:21.200
You're saying that he'll understand 
who it was for in the end, right?

18:21.200 --> 18:24.990
He's a pastor, but he can't even 
understand how Cecilia feels?

18:24.990 --> 18:27.440
And when he's perfect 
at everything else, too.

18:27.440 --> 18:30.120
Makes things tougher on everyone around him.

18:30.750 --> 18:33.460
Oh, if it isn't the pastor!

18:33.460 --> 18:34.740
Miss Fortune Teller!

18:34.740 --> 18:36.250
You can call me Mell.

18:36.250 --> 18:38.090
The lady saint isn't with you?

18:38.090 --> 18:41.080
Well, today is Valentine's Day.

18:41.080 --> 18:43.640
She's working hard at making chocolates.

18:43.640 --> 18:45.530
Really? That's great!

18:45.530 --> 18:46.140
What?

18:46.140 --> 18:49.280
Well, the lady saint is devoting herself 
to tackling the challenge, right?

18:49.280 --> 18:52.560
Taking action for someone 
else's sake is really important.

18:54.160 --> 18:56.450
Yes... you're right.

18:57.140 --> 18:59.880
I'm worried about how 
the lady saint might be doing, so...

18:59.880 --> 19:01.990
Sure. Bye-bye.

19:02.390 --> 19:03.330
Huh?

19:03.330 --> 19:05.500
Did he get the wrong idea about something?

19:07.240 --> 19:10.500
<i>To think that the lady saint 
has had her eye on someone.</i>

19:10.880 --> 19:13.260
<i>I really didn't notice at all.</i>

19:14.490 --> 19:17.000
Lady Saint? I bought ingredients for...

19:18.500 --> 19:20.160
Welcome home.

19:20.160 --> 19:23.930
Um, how does a person get bleeding to stop?

19:27.080 --> 19:29.730
If we do this, I think 
the bleeding should stop.

19:29.730 --> 19:30.770
All right.

19:30.770 --> 19:33.470
<i>I shouldn't have left her alone!</i>

19:33.470 --> 19:34.840
Lady Saint,

19:34.840 --> 19:37.640
there's no need to push yourself this hard
to make chocolates, is there?

19:37.640 --> 19:39.170
Continuing like this will be—

19:39.170 --> 19:40.320
No.

19:41.110 --> 19:44.330
I must make something proper and acceptable.

19:45.240 --> 19:47.080
I see.

19:47.750 --> 19:51.080
<i>She said that she wouldn't let me be alone,</i>

19:51.080 --> 19:53.800
<i>but it might not stay that way forever.</i>

19:54.320 --> 19:57.080
<i>She might come to need 
someone other than me.</i>

19:57.080 --> 19:59.920
<i>If the lady saint left, too...</i>

20:00.440 --> 20:03.510
<i>this place would feel lonely again.</i>

20:05.960 --> 20:08.470
I finally succeeded!

20:08.470 --> 20:10.400
I'm mentally exhausted.

20:10.400 --> 20:12.480
Lawren, did this make you ill?

20:12.480 --> 20:15.020
Oh, right? Would you like to wrap it?

20:15.020 --> 20:16.640
No.

20:16.640 --> 20:19.200
I'll give it now, just as it is.

20:19.200 --> 20:19.900
What?

20:19.900 --> 20:23.450
I made it to give to you, Lawren.

20:23.450 --> 20:27.340
I don't know if it tastes good or not, 
but will you please accept it?

20:27.990 --> 20:30.040
I-I'm so sorry!

20:31.750 --> 20:35.120
You learned how to make it 
from the person you wanted to give it to?

20:35.850 --> 20:37.450
Yes, I did.

20:37.450 --> 20:40.710
I thought there was someone else 
you were going to give it to.

20:41.290 --> 20:43.010
You really thought that?!

20:43.010 --> 20:45.090
Well, since you asked me how to make it,

20:45.090 --> 20:46.430
of course that's what I thought.

20:46.430 --> 20:49.760
B-But... the person I want to give it to,

20:49.760 --> 20:51.480
and the person I rely on most...

20:51.480 --> 20:54.980
for me, both of those people are you, Lawren.

20:56.880 --> 20:58.360
Um...

20:59.780 --> 21:01.600
Thank you.

21:01.900 --> 21:03.070
<i>Thump</i>

21:02.930 --> 21:05.160
<i>I'm so glad I made it!</i>

21:05.600 --> 21:08.240
So you still need me, then?

21:08.240 --> 21:08.810
What?

21:08.810 --> 21:10.840
Oh! No, it's nothing!

21:10.840 --> 21:12.900
Wait, this means it's my fault 
that your finger is—

21:12.900 --> 21:14.280
'Tis a wound gained for glory!

21:14.280 --> 21:16.160
This will bring you glory?

21:16.160 --> 21:21.010
I-I think that depends 
on how you respond, Lawren.

21:21.010 --> 21:22.050
Oh!

21:22.050 --> 21:23.810
How much should I repay you with?

21:23.810 --> 21:27.800
<i>Should I just assume that this is 
because he's so dense?</i>

21:27.800 --> 21:29.600
You made her cry, didn't you?

21:29.600 --> 21:30.840
Miss Hazelita?

21:30.840 --> 21:33.350
Lawrence! What sort of person are you?

21:33.350 --> 21:36.260
Couldn't you just accept properly, 
just today of all days?

21:36.640 --> 21:39.780
Look at how hard Cecilia worked on this!

21:36.640 --> 21:39.780
Oh, dear. Miss, stop. Stop.

21:39.780 --> 21:41.830
Honestly, do you really not understand?

21:41.830 --> 21:44.940
<i>It seems my feelings didn't reach him,</i>

21:44.940 --> 21:48.440
<i>but getting to see expressions of Lawren's 
that he doesn't usually show...</i>

21:48.440 --> 21:50.490
<i>was enough for me today.</i>

23:20.970 --> 23:25.450
I've heard there's a pressure point in the hand
 that relieves vehicle-related motion sickness.

23:25.450 --> 23:27.720
Let's see. If I'm right... it's here!

23:27.590 --> 23:28.970
<b>Stab!</b>

23:27.720 --> 23:28.970
There?!

23:29.220 --> 23:30.780
I thought it was gonna break.

23:30.780 --> 23:32.490
It seems like it worked.

23:32.490 --> 23:35.230
Lady Saint, did you get sick 
from riding the cart?

23:35.230 --> 23:38.140
I may have, so please press away!

23:38.140 --> 23:39.530
You look like you feel fine!

23:39.530 --> 23:41.530

